<article class="env-lemma" id="0D1I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D1I">Lemma <span data-tag="0D1I">99.13.6</span>.</a> The stack $p'_{fp, flat, proper} : \mathcal{S}\! \mathit{paces}'_{fp, flat, proper} \to \mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ is limit preserving (Artin's Axioms, Definition <a href="/tag/07XL" data-tag="07XL">98.11.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i$ be the limits of a directed inverse system of affine schemes. By Limits of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07SK" data-tag="07SK">70.7.1</a> the category of algebraic spaces of finite presentation over $T$ is the colimit of the categories of algebraic spaces of finite presentation over $T_ i$. To finish the proof use that flatness and properness descends through the limit, see Limits of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/08K0" data-tag="08K0">70.6.12</a> and <a href="/tag/08K1" data-tag="08K1">70.6.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>